  "deviations": [
    {
      "achieved": null,
      "declared": "exact",
      "description": "prediction with a last batch of a single row completes (1) or raises (0)",
      "detail": "",
      "explanation": "1.6.1 collects `outputs.squeeze()` per prediction batch and concatenates them. A last batch of one row squeezes to a zero-dimensional array and `np.concatenate` raises `ValueError: zero-dimensional arrays cannot be concatenated`; the same happens for a dataset of one pair. v2 predicts through `predict_pairs`, which keeps the batch dimension. Case: the batch size is one less than the number of test pairs.",
      "max_abs_diff": 1.0,
      "max_rel_diff": 1.0,
      "name": "tail_batch/completes",
      "passed": false,
      "pearson": null,
      "scope": "deviation",
      "shape_v1": [],
      "shape_v2": []
    }
  ],
  "findings": [
    "The ontology reading is the 1.6.1 one: `load_mapping`, `load_ontology`, `sort_pairs` and `pairs_in_layers` produce the same per-layer pairs (virtual nodes for non-adjacent edges included) and the same connectivity (`indices` buffers) from the same files. v2 reads the text from `mdata.uns['sparsego']` (`{'ontology': ..., 'gene2ind': ...}`) instead of `sparseGO_ont.txt` / `gene2ind.txt` next to the CSVs, and validates more (it raises on terms without genes, several roots, several components, non-contiguous gene indices; 1.6.1 prints and goes on).",
    "The network, the SGD loop (momentum 0.9, learning rate `lr / (1 + decay_rate * epoch)` set per epoch) and the network construction at the start of `train` are the 1.6.1 ones: with the same seed the initial weights, the shuffling and the dropout masks agree and the trained parameters and predictions agree at the `train` class.",
    "v2 defaults (`SparseGO` predictor, commit 174ceea7, B5) are the first grid point of the 1.6.1 `hyperparameters.yaml` (`num_neurons_per_final_GO` 30, `num_neurons_drug` [100, 50, 6], `p_drop_*` 0.15, `epochs` 400, `batch_size` 20000), not the defaults of the 1.6.1 class (6, [200, 100, 50], 0.1, 100, 10000). The case sets every hyperparameter explicitly on both sides.",
    "v2 selects the ontology genes by name from the `gene_expression` / `mutations` view and raises if one is missing, as the 1.6.1 loader does; the preset has no gene list (1.6.1 loads `gene_list=None`, all columns, then restricts to `gene2ind`).",
    "The model keeps the last epoch on both sides (no early stopping, no checkpoint)."
  ],
